  "scope": "Reference retention-batch selection, preflight and commit coordination. Native owners retain maps, bounded measurement, SQL, complete-group deletion checks, transaction lifetime and audit cascades.",
  "limitations": [
    "The frozen memory and durable batch bodies come from 63df912e and are unaffected by the preceding uncommitted sequence-gate slice. They do not call migrated compaction policy. Native storage, bounded measurement and complete-group deletion helpers remain shared.",
    "The 240 memory cases cover twelve local/group/payload variants, five retention ceilings and four batch sizes. They compare exact reports/errors and all maps, preserve duplicate/local order behavior, and confirm no mutation on late measurement refusal.",
    "The 360 SQLite cases cover four source forms, three lifecycle stages, ten storage/trigger variants and three policies. Corrupt fixture admission is disabled only during setup; these fixtures are not supported recovery checkpoints. Candidate row ordering and all production SQL predicates remain unchanged.",
    "Nine direct adapter tests cover protection, numeric-age ordering, full preflight, saturating counts, no-removal reconciliation, native fault ownership, unwind/drop ordering, invalid counts/kinds/delete cardinality and empty candidate batches without retries.",
    "A public two-worker case reconciles stale local completed entries after a peer removes a whole group, then reopens without redispatch or identity reuse. A second public case proves a late group-branch deletion failure rolls back earlier standalone deletion without cache eviction; removal of the injected failure permits retry and reopen.",
    "Memory continues to order by continuation age and measure logical payloads; SQLite continues to order by native row age and count stored bytes. Their different accounting and reconciliation semantics are preserved, not unified or promoted as host-neutral recovery.",
    "Native complete-group deletion validation, byte-accounting internals and cache publication ownership remain in place. This slice adds no format migration, admission bypass, compensating write, retry or independent transaction.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, actual exported-source execution, complete independent durable recovery, power-loss, disk-full, multi-host race or performance evidence is claimed."
  ],
